%% Signals Flow Diagram - V2 (Detailed Technical Flow)
graph TD
    subgraph Admin Action
        A["<i class='fa fa-user-shield'></i> 1. Admin updates a specific<br>Permission instance (ID=42)<br>in Django Admin"]
    end

    subgraph Django ORM & Signals
        B["<i class='fa fa-save'></i> 2. `ElementPermissionsUser.objects.get(id=42).save()` is triggered"]
        C["<i class='fa fa-bell'></i> 3. Django's Signal dispatcher sends a 'post_save' signal<br>passing the saved `instance` (ID=42)"]
        D["<i class='fa fa-cogs'></i> 4. `on_permission_save(instance, ...)` handler is invoked"]
    end

    subgraph Signal Handler Logic
        E["<i class='fa fa-code'></i> 5. Inside the handler:<br> - A group name is constructed using the instance ID<br>  `group_name = f'perm_{instance.id}'` => 'perm_42'"]
        F["<i class='fa fa-paper-plane'></i> 6. A message payload is created<br>containing the updated permission data"]
        G["<i class='fa fa-broadcast-tower'></i> 7. `channel_layer.group_send('perm_42', payload)` is called"]
    end
    
    subgraph Real-time Layer (Redis)
        H["<i class='fa fa-exchange-alt'></i> 8. The message is published on the 'perm_42' channel<br>in Redis Pub/Sub"]
    end

    subgraph Consumer Side
        I["<i class='fa fa-user-cog'></i> 9. Browser Consumers subscribed to 'perm_42'<br>receive the message"]
        J["<i class='fa fa-sync-alt'></i> 10. The consumer's `permissions_updates` method is executed"]
        K["<i class='fa fa-desktop'></i> 11. Consumer sends a formatted update<br>to the specific browser client via WebSocket"]
    end

    subgraph End Result
        L["<i class='fa fa-check-square'></i> 12. Browser UI reacts to the message,<br>updating the dashboard in real-time"]
    end

    %% Connect the stages
    A --> B
    B --> C
    C --> D
    D --> E
    E --> F
    F --> G
    G --> H
    H --> I
    I --> J
    J --> K
    K --> L